- [x] Feature

## Description of change

- Adapters can provide a new method `paapiParameters`, which takes the same argument as `buildRequests`, and should return an object mapping arbitrary names to PAAPI asynchronous parameters (currently, auction nonces and B&A auction data).
- If paapi is enabled for a bidder, its `bidderRequest.paapi.createAuctionNonce` and `.getInterestGroupAdAuctionData` can be used to ask for the corresponding navigator APIs,
- the parameters are resolved and populated in `bidderRequest.paapi.params` before `buildPaapiConfigs` and `buildRequests`.

For example:

```javascript
registerBidder({
    paapiParameters(validBidRequests, bidderRequest) {
        return {
             nonce: bidderRequest.paapi.createAuctionNonce(),
             igData: bidderRequest.paapi.getInterestGroupAdAuctionData(...)
        }
    }, 
    buildPAAPIConfigs(validBidRequests, bidderRequest) {
         const {nonce, igData} = bidderRequest.paapi.params;
         // here (and in `buildRequests`) nonce and igData are resolved return values from those navigator APIs
    }
})
```

## Other information

Closes https://github.com/prebid/Prebid.js/issues/10740

## Breaking changes

### formAction always returns the mutation result

Now we always return the full `MutationResult` on `formAction`. If you use `formAction` without a `successPath` and manually get the action data in your components, you'll have to check for `success` first and only then access the mutation result inside `data`:

```tsx
export const action = async ({ request }: Route.ActionArgs) =>
  formAction({ request, schema, mutation })

export default function Component({ actionData }: Route.ComponentProps) {
  if (!actionData) {
    return <p>Our action has not run yet.</p>
  }

  if (!actionData.success) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h3>Errors:</h3>
        <pre>{JSON.stringify(actionData.errors, null, 2)}</pre>
        <h3>Values:</h3>
        <pre>{JSON.stringify(actionData.values, null, 2)}</pre>
      </div>
    )
  }

  return (
    <div>
      <h3>Data:</h3>
      <pre>{JSON.stringify(actionData.data, null, 2)}</pre>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### formAction returns 422 status on failed mutations

To avoid revalidating loaders unnecessarily, `formAction` now returns a 422 status on failed mutations.

